  "question": {
    "text": "If the radius of a star is $R$ and it acts as a black body, what would be the temperature of the star, in which the rate of energy production is $Q$ ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$Q / 4 \\pi R^{2} \\sigma$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\mathrm{Q} / 4 \\pi R^{2} \\sigma\\right)^{-1 / 2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(4 \\pi R^{2} Q / \\sigma\\right)^{1 / 4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\mathrm{Q} / 4 \\pi R^{2} \\sigma\\right)^{1 / 4}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Stefan's law for black bodyradiation $Q=\\sigma e A T^{4}$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nT=\\left[\\frac{Q}{\\sigma\\left(4 \\pi R^{2}\\right)}\\right]^{1 / 4}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nHere $e=1$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nA=4 \\pi R^{2}\r\n\r\n$$"
  }
